window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"sett","b":"locke","win":["Sett","Sett","Sett","Sett","Skill","Skill","Sett"],"spikes":[{"when":"Level 1","text":"Grit shield plus heavy autos turn his trades against him from the opening wave."},{"when":"Level 3","text":"Knuckle Down slow into Facebreaker pins him for the full combo — your kill window opens."},{"when":"Locke level 6","text":"Purgatory brings his first real threat — stop brawling at execute-range HP."},{"when":"Two-plus items","text":"Haymaker true-damage returns and the R suppress make committing into you a losing bet."}],"wants":{"you":["Auto trades that feed Grit and Haymaker","Facebreaker landed on his dash path","HP kept out of execute range after his 6"],"foe":["A low-HP target for the Purgatory slow-in","Your Haymaker baited and side-stepped","Even stages turned into burst coinflips"]},"early":"The first five levels are a bully window: Grit shields his damage into Haymaker fuel, your heavy autos win every exchange, and level-3 Knuckle Down into Facebreaker pins him for the whole combo. He wants poke-and-retreat; give him nothing but face-to-face brawls he cannot afford.","mid":"At 6 and his first item, the lane briefly evens: Purgatory gives him a genuine execute, so keep your HP honest and never let a slow-in start while you are low. Keep trading in short bursts that bank Grit, and remember the even window is his best one — your scaling closes it soon.","late":"Late game committing into you becomes a losing proposition for him: the Haymaker true-damage return punishes his burst and The Show Stopper suppress deletes his one commitment. Frontline fights, suppress his engage, and walk him into your team — his execute cannot find a threshold on a full-HP Sett.","whys":["Your level-1 Grit shield and heavy autos turn his trades against him immediately.","At 2 your auto pressure and shield keep you ahead in every exchange he takes.","Level 3 Knuckle Down slow into Facebreaker pins him for your full combo.","Through 4-5 your stored Haymaker punishes his burst with a true-damage return.","At 6 it briefly evens: his ult threat forces you to respect the execute window.","First item stays even-ish — his burst arrives before your R suppress and tankiness take over.","Late your Haymaker return and R suppress make committing into you a loss — the duel is yours."]});
