window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"sett","b":"zaahen","win":["Skill","Sett","Sett","Skill","Skill","Zaahen","Zaahen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Level 2","text":"Early Q-W pressure starts winning the short trades — open the bully window."},{"when":"Level 3","text":"Shield-punch Haymaker plus your engage own the lane — this is your best stage."},{"when":"Zaahen first item","text":"The lane flips: his sustain outlasts your plateauing burst from here on."},{"when":"Zaahen two items","text":"His sustained output grinds you down — your lead must already be spent."}],"wants":{"you":["Heavy trades cashed during levels 2-3","A lead converted to plates and roams","The game ended before his item spikes"],"foe":["A quiet lane into first item","Extended brawls his Q and R heal through","Late sidelane duels you cannot win"]},"early":"Level 1 is even, then your bully window opens: Q-W pressure wins the short trades at 2, and at 3 the shield-punch Haymaker plus your engage own the lane outright. Cash this window hard — chunk him, force his sums wrong, and take plates — because 4-5 evens out once his combo comes online.","mid":"Level 6 stays even: your R and full combo genuinely match his all-in, so the stage belongs to whoever engages smarter. But his first item is the turn — his sustain starts outlasting your plateauing burst. Spend your lead now: roam, dive with your jungler, and drag the game toward a close.","late":"Two items in, his sustained output grinds you down and the sidelane duel is his. Shift jobs: you are now the teamfight engage. Suppress the highest-value target with The Show Stopper, wall-slam into your team, and let Haymaker clear the frontline — just never queue up for the 1v1 he wants.","whys":["Level 1 is an even skill lane before Grit and combos matter to either side.","At 2 your early Q-W pressure starts winning the short trades — the bully window opens.","By 3 your shield-punch Haymaker and engage own the lane — your strongest stage.","Levels 4-5 read even as his combo comes online and starts contesting you.","Level 6 stays even: your R and combo match his all-in blow for blow.","His first item flips it — his sustain outlasts your plateauing burst.","With two items his sustained output grinds down a bully who is out of steam — avoid the duel."]});
